= 20.1 release (2026-06-15)

 * Various bug fixes and improvments
 * improvments on the sensitivity analysis wizard
 * added the possibility to duplicate a data set
 * multiple selection now working in paraview graphs
 * computations can be interrupted with ydefx

= 20.0 release (2026-03-30)

 * added HSIC sensitivity analyses
 * made simulation analyses export to data model possible
 * moved some analyses from physical models to data sets (SRC, metamodels)
 * added a type parameter for data models
 * added a button to install python packages
 * added the possibility to continue Monte Carlo analysis even if some points failed
 * Various bug fixes

= 19.1 release (2025-12-5)

 * Various ergonomics improvements including
   * A new button to copy the distributions selected for a marginal to all the other ones in inference
   * The possibility to load the mesh along with the data for fields data set
   * Making probabilistic and Monte-Carlo the default choices for DOE creation
 * Added the possibility to run coupling models on remote machines via SSH
 * Added plain regression analysis and advanced parameters for stepwise regression
 * changed default installation path on windows in user mode
 * Various bug fixes

= 19.0 release (2025-10-10)

 * Added sensitivity analysis for data models using rank Sobol/SRC indices
 * Allow to use Student copula in dependency inference
 * Added Histogram distribution
 * Added a button to create a python model encapsulating a metamodel
 * Data analyses can now be performed on datasets containing missing/nan values
 * Design of experiments of simulation analyses can now be exported
 * Added the possibility to import evaluations for a design of experiments
 * Added the possibility to display full plot matrix when using ParaView
 * Default block size is set to the number of processors
 * Improve YACS integration
 * Print stack traces to console and archive them in text files for debugging purposes
 * Various bug fixes

= 18.1 release (2025-06-25)

 * Consistent metamodel error measures (MSE, R2)
 * New CSV parser from OpenTURNS 1.25 allowing missing values, unicode chars
 * Coupling model fixes
 * Boost dependency is now optional (only required for nsis installer)
 * Probabilistic model is now exported when creating a metamodel with FCE from a data model
 * Various bug fixes

= 18.0 release (2025-04-02)

 * Quantile analysis
 * DataFieldModel fixes
 * Various bug fixes

= 17.0 release (2024-10-11)

 * Added global parallelization setting
